  "text": "Assistance Needed with Pharmacy Substitution Messaging and Out-of-Stock Protocols\n\nHello Support, our clinical team is encountering several out-of-stock notices from local pharmacies and we need guidance on how to properly execute therapeutic alternative switches within the software. Specifically, when we receive a pharmacy notification stating a drug is unavailable, we attempt to navigate to the prescribing module to select an alternative agent, but the messaging workflow for substitution does not seem to transmit our instructions correctly back to the pharmacist. We have tried cancelling and re-issuing the electronic order using standard dropdowns, yet the pharmacy continues to report receiving ambiguous status codes. Could you please provide detailed instructions or documentation on the correct sequence for handling these substitution alerts so our providers can clear their pending queues efficiently?"
 },
